## Key Findings and Learning Outcomes

This project demonstrates how machine learning can support fraud detection. It highlights the importance of handling imbalanced datasets and selecting evaluation metrics that reflect the real problem.

The project also provides practical experience with data preprocessing, Random Forest classification, model evaluation, and the trade-offs between detecting more fraudulent transactions and minimizing false alarms.

